    "text": "&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0032997_ANs.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 184px;\" /><br /><br /><strong>i)</strong> In this case of current will flow from B top A. No current will flow through branch C, E (as marked in figure)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>eq</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><strong>ii)</strong> Here current will flow from A to B so no current will flow in branch D<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>eq</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></math><br /><br /><strong>iii)</strong> Here also current will flow from A to B, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>eq</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;same as (ii)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>ii</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>iii&#160;</mtext></msub><msub><mtext>&#60;&#160;R</mtext><mtext>i</mtext></msub></math>",
